# orbit_camera · a film camera that circles one point, slowly and all the way round, again and again
# orbit_camera(around, radius, height, seconds, lens) makes the scene a film (`mode "movie"`) with one shot that goes
# once round `around` in `seconds` (30), `radius` metres out (6) and `height` metres up (2.2), always looking at a
# point a metre above it, then starts again with no jolt. Drop it on the middle of what you want to show.
# kind: script
# place: orbit_camera(AT)
# credit: J Production, made in Loop3D
# licence: our own work, free for every J Production project
# from: the library's Scripts shelf (2026-11-23)
# tags: camera, orbit, turntable, film, showcase, circle, script
to orbit_camera(around: vec(0, 0, 0), radius: 6, height: 2.2, seconds: 30, lens: 35 mm)
  mode "movie"
  orbit("round", seconds, around: around, radius: radius, height: height, from: 0 deg, to: 360 deg, lens: lens, look_at: around + vec(0, 1, 0), ease: "linear")
